  data: {
    LLM: 'Each player receives 13 cards and arranges them into three hands face down: back hand (5 cards, strongest), middle hand (5 cards, middle strength), front hand (3 cards, weakest). Back must beat middle, middle must beat front. Players expose hands simultaneously. Each pair of players compares corresponding hands, winning one unit per hand beaten.',
    Player: 'Each player receives 13 cards and arranges them into three hands face down: back hand (5 cards, strongest), middle hand (5 cards, middle strength), front hand (3 cards, weakest). Back must beat middle, middle must beat front. Players expose hands simultaneously. Each pair of players compares corresponding hands, winning one unit per hand beaten.',
    objective: "Arrange 13 cards into three poker hands (back: 5 cards, middle: 5 cards, front: 3 cards) where back ≥ middle ≥ front in strength. Win units by beating opponents' corresponding hands.",
    gameplay: 'Each player receives 13 cards and arranges them into three hands face down: back hand (5 cards, strongest), middle hand (5 cards, middle strength), front hand (3 cards, weakest). Back must beat middle, middle must beat front. Players expose hands simultaneously. Each pair of players compares corresponding hands, winning one unit per hand beaten.',
