      'Setup example: 5 card(s) per player.',
      "Rule example: Arrange 13 cards into three poker hands (back: 5 cards, middle: 5 cards, front: 3 cards) where back ≥ middle ≥ front in strength. Win units by beating opponents' corresponding hands.",
      'Turn-flow example: Each player receives 13 cards and arranges them into three hands face down: back hand (5 cards, strongest), middle hand (5 cards, middle strength), front hand (3 cards, weakest). Back must beat middle, middle must beat front. Players expose hands simultaneously. Each pair of players compares corresponding hands, winning one unit per hand beaten.',
      "Scoring example: Basic scoring: Win 1 unit for each corresponding hand you beat, lose 1 unit for each hand that beats you. Special hands: Three of a kind in front wins 3 units instead of 1. Full house in middle wins 2 units. Four of a kind in back/middle wins 4 units. Royal/straight flush in back/middle wins 5 units. Special 13-card hands win automatically: Six pairs (3 units), Three straights (3 units), Three flushes (3 units), Complete straight A-K (13 units). Arrange 13 cards into three poker hands (back: 5 cards, middle: 5 cards, front: 3 cards) where back ≥ middle ≥ front in strength. Win units by beating opponents' corresponding hands..",
